## Introduction

# Introduction

## Sequence 1 — Opening crawl

BLACK.

A child's quiet intake of breath.

Stars appear. Music swells with warmth and a sense of discovery.

HAPPY BEINGS

EPISODE IV — NEW HORIZONS

The title recedes into the stars. An opening crawl follows, rising slowly into
the distance in the manner of Star Wars. Each paragraph appears in time with
the child's reading; allow enough time to read and listen comfortably.

The child speaks naturally, with the curiosity of someone telling us about home.

<!-- Previous narrator cue: CHILD (V.O.) — CRAWL TEXT -->

Bee is heard only in voice-over. He remains unseen; his name and identity are not revealed to the audience.

**BEE (V.O.) — CRAWL TEXT**

On Earth, we stopped using money so long ago that most of us have forgotten it.

I saw some once, in a history lesson. Little metal circles. Pieces of paper.
Numbers on a screen. It was strange to think you might need those things before
someone would give you food.

Now we grow things, build things, and share what we know. We look after each
other because we care. There are no wars anymore.

We still have things to learn. Sometimes it takes a lot of talking to
understand one another.

Our cities float on the sea. Our ships travel between planets. Humans, robots,
androids, and cyborgs live and explore together. There are so many ways to be
someone.

Years ago, a ship called First Horizon reached a planet we call XYZ. Its crew
sent word of breathable air, oceans, and two moons.

Then their messages stopped. The ship disappeared.

There were friends on that ship.

Now Second Horizon is going to look for them.

**END CRAWL**

The last words drift out of sight. The music softens.

## Sequence 2 — Into the journey

EXT. SPACE

Hold on the stars.

<!-- Previous transition preserved:
SECOND HORIZON glides into view, small against the vastness. We move towards it.

Ahead lies XYZ.
-->

Earth comes into view, blue and sunlit. We move towards its oceans and a city floating on the water.

At the harbour, SECOND HORIZON waits for departure.

The sound of the sea carries us into morning.

CONTINUE INTO: THE DEPARTURE

<!-- Previous Introduction preserved for future development.

# Introduction

This is the book about universes without money and at this place you actually could close the book, because it is really what in the essence the book is about or you can keep reading about the characters and their journeys in these universes as the saga tells some stories about several various wonderful beings.

Some of the characters of the story are: an intersex being, an artificially created / grown female being with enhanced features and capabilities, a gorgeous and stunningly beautiful transwoman and absolutely “normal” male being, an older male, a "child", several lovers and other wonderful beings of all possible body types and colours. There are blue beings, yellow and multicoloured beings in the story, a blue moon and an orange moon, which change their colours and vast cosmos with it’s endless stars and universes.

The main objective of the book is to show you as a reader that living a free and happy life in the world where money doesn't exist even as a term is not only, but absolutely possible and hopefully you can read in the book how you, yes you the one, who is reading this book, can come to such a (way of) living, too.

If you want to contribute to the story you can. Please read README for more information.
If you want to contribute to the story you can. Please read README for more information. 

-->

